FastSASA Notices
==============

FastSASA is a GPU-accelerated SASA implementation with Vulkan, CUDA, and
threaded CPU backends. Its kernels, shaders, CPU fallback, trajectory
engine, parsers, and command-line implementation are FastSASA-owned.

Bundled radius table
---------------------

The standard residue/atom mappings in `share/protor.config`, and the same base
mappings reused by `share/protor_glycans.config`, derive from the generated
ProtOr configuration distributed by FreeSASA (Mitternacht S. FreeSASA: An
open source C library for solvent accessible surface area calculations.
F1000Research 2016, 5:189). The underlying ProtOr radii are from Tsai J,
Taylor R, Chothia C, Gerstein M. J Mol Biol. 1999;290:253-266. The glycan
mappings in
`share/protor_glycans.config` are a FastSASA opt-in extension; that file is not
an unmodified upstream file.
The per-residue maximum-ASA reference table used for relative SASA
(`--format rsa`, in `tools/fastsasa_cli.cc`) is FreeSASA's own ProtOr
reference values, reproduced in FastSASA-native source rather than as a
separate config file. FastSASA does not compile, link, or vendor the
FreeSASA CPU implementation itself. It contains only the attributed reference
data described above.

